Z||000000||deceler8||08-26-2000||10:48 AM||||There was a story recently on the news about the wierdest things ever put in a dishwasher...it was a story about how Whirlpool tested their dishwashers to ensure long life...<P>Usual stuff like people poaching salmon or washing baseball caps...pretty lame stuff.<P>I've got them all beat...used my dishwasher to clean a transmission and case from my 1951 Chevy pickup that I was rebuilding. Worked like a charm.<P>Actually it was a new dishwasher in a brand new house, and we moved 9 months later.<P>Can anyone top that ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||08-26-2000||11:21 AM||||Hmm. I thought when I used my wife's scum buster to polish my 454's pistons was pretty good. But you win!||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-27-2000||02:35 PM||||I've washed a bunch of differant things in "dish" washers. Lots of cicuit boards. A few other things.... That's about the biggest thing I've heard of going in one.<P>You have to watch what you use for soap.... that dishwasher soap can wreck circuit boards.<P>We used to take all the discard AV stuff and whatever else and use it for target practic. That was always a fun way to end a summer.||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||08-27-2000||02:58 PM||||i hear that some people cook fish in their dishwasher.  Somthing about wraping them in foil and then a plastic bag to make it waterproof.  My wife hasn't let me try it so I don't know how well it works.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||08-28-2000||01:02 PM||||I used the electric oven in my old house to bake the  paint on a set of rally wheels. (Didn't do much cooking.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>When I die, I want to go peacefully, in my sleep, like Grandpa.<BR>Not screaming, like the passengers in his car.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||1
